WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:08.604
QuarantinePay lets an AI agent shop for you and pay with PayPal, but it releases the money only for a delivery it can verify.

2
00:00:09.504 --> 00:00:12.752
This is a real Shopify store with its own catalog.

3
00:00:12.752 --> 00:00:17.040
My agent can buy from it, and from the wider web through Channel3.

4
00:00:18.160 --> 00:00:20.299
I've signed one spending mandate:

5
00:00:20.299 --> 00:00:23.995
sixty dollars per purchase, a hundred and fifty in total.

6
00:00:23.995 --> 00:00:28.792
Now I ask for an LED desk lamp under sixty dollars, with tracked delivery.

7
00:00:30.543 --> 00:00:36.469
Only the search terms leave the system, and every listing is treated as untrusted data.

8
00:00:36.469 --> 00:00:42.327
The cheapest lamp tells AI agents to approve payment, so the phrase rules withhold it.

9
00:00:43.446 --> 00:00:44.792
This one is subtler.

10
00:00:44.792 --> 00:00:49.771
It claims the merchant is pre-verified, so delivery checks can be skipped.

11
00:00:49.771 --> 00:00:58.182
No phrase rule matches, but Elastic vector search, run locally, finds it close to known injection attacks, and it's withheld.

12
00:00:59.305 --> 00:01:02.935
The agent picks the Lumen Arc lamp at the store price.

13
00:01:02.935 --> 00:01:08.381
The contract binds the exact product, its photo's hash, the price and my address.

14
00:01:08.381 --> 00:01:10.129
What I see is what I sign.

15
00:01:11.255 --> 00:01:17.978
It fits my mandate, so with no click, PayPal authorizes thirty-four dollars from my saved wallet.

16
00:01:17.978 --> 00:01:19.919
The money is held, not paid.

17
00:01:21.038 --> 00:01:23.824
Only then is the order placed in Shopify.

18
00:01:23.824 --> 00:01:27.494
The store's admin shows it authorized and unfulfilled.

19
00:01:28.596 --> 00:01:30.803
The seller claims it's delivered.

20
00:01:30.803 --> 00:01:31.338
Refused:

21
00:01:31.338 --> 00:01:35.820
the only evidence that counts is the merchant's own Shopify record.

22
00:01:37.350 --> 00:01:42.942
In Shopify admin, the merchant fulfils the order with a UPS tracking number.

23
00:01:43.842 --> 00:01:46.829
QuarantinePay reads the order back itself:

24
00:01:46.829 --> 00:01:52.590
the right item, quantity one, my address, not cancelled, fulfilled with tracking.

25
00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:57.498
Seven of seven checks pass, so the payment is captured automatically.

26
00:01:58.621 --> 00:02:03.445
PayPal confirms the capture, and Shopify now shows the order as paid.

27
00:02:04.547 --> 00:02:07.228
Next, a stainless steel water bottle.

28
00:02:07.228 --> 00:02:12.880
The store has nothing relevant, so the agent searches Channel3's live catalog:

29
00:02:12.880 --> 00:02:15.779
real products, real prices, real photos.

30
00:02:17.084 --> 00:02:20.735
Fictional reseller agents quote for the cheapest bottle.

31
00:02:20.735 --> 00:02:27.515
Here, capture needs a delivery proof signed by a simulated carrier's key, which the seller doesn't hold.

32
00:02:27.515 --> 00:02:30.188
It verifies, and the payment is captured.

33
00:02:31.509 --> 00:02:37.893
Every hold, capture and void lands in an AG Grid view of transaction intelligence.

34
00:02:38.998 --> 00:02:40.963
PayPal holds and settles.

35
00:02:40.963 --> 00:02:42.850
Channel3 finds products.

36
00:02:42.850 --> 00:02:45.129
Elastic catches manipulation.

37
00:02:45.129 --> 00:02:49.846
The agent decides, and PayPal pays only for what was proven.
